{
  "id": "extensive_game.perfect_information.zero_sum_perfect_information_value",
  "title": "Value In Finite Zero-Sum Perfect-Information Games",
  "kind": "theorem",
  "status": "staged",
  "href": "extensive_game/perfect_information/extensive_game_perfect_information_zero_sum_perfect_information_value.html",
  "body_html": "<h1>Value In Finite Zero-Sum Perfect-Information Games</h1>\n<p>Every finite zero-sum perfect-information game, with or without Nature, has a\nvalue and both players have pure optimal strategies.</p>",
  "proof_html": "<p>Sketch</p>\n<p>Use forward induction on the tree. If Nature moves at the root, the value is the\nprobability-weighted average of the successor subgame values. If player 1 moves,\nthe value is the maximum of successor values; if player 2 moves, it is the minimum.\nOptimal pure strategies are obtained by choosing an optimal successor and then\nfollowing optimal strategies in the selected subgame.</p>",
